        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Deep Purple, Led Zeppelin, Black Sabbath\n- Albums: 24 Carat Purple, BBC Sessions 1968–1970\n- Places: BBC Maida Vale Studios\n- Concepts: unholy trinity of British hard rock and heavy metal\n\nFacts:\n- Deep Purple released the album 24 Carat Purple.\n- Deep Purple, Led Zeppelin, and Black Sabbath were referred to as the \"unholy trinity of British hard rock and heavy metal in the early to mid-seventies\".\n- A performance by Deep Purple was featured on the 2011 compilation album BBC Sessions 1968–1970.\n- BBC Sessions 1968–1970 featured studio performances recorded at BBC Maida Vale Studios.",
