        "original_id": "fc1cf9e3-52c2-58a4-abb7-3890d0243237",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: BBC Sessions 1968–1970, 24 Carat Purple\n- People: Deep Purple\n- Organizations: BBC\n- Places: Maida Vale Studios, London\n- Topics: British hard rock, heavy metal\n\nFacts:\n- Deep Purple’s performances were recorded at the BBC’s Maida Vale Studios in London and originally broadcast on various BBC Radio shows from 1968 through 1970.\n- Deep Purple, together with Led Zeppelin and Black Sabbath, have been referred to as the \"unholy trinity of British hard rock and heavy metal\" in the early to mid-1970s.\n- BBC Sessions 1968–1970 is a 2011 studio compilation album featuring Deep Purple performances recorded for the BBC.\n- 24 Carat Purple is the first Deep Purple compilation album released worldwide on the band’s own record company and the third album in the band’s compilation series.",
